# GitHub token used by the local helper scripts:
# - `pnpm github:selfhosted:start|stop|status`
# - `pnpm github:selfhosted:enable|disable`
#
# Recommended: classic PAT with `repo` scope (works reliably with Actions runner + variables APIs).
#
# Fine-grained PATs can also work, but orgs may require approval/SSO authorization.
# If you see `Resource not accessible by personal access token`, use a classic PAT or approve/authorize the fine-grained PAT.
#
# Fine-grained PAT permissions (when allowed):
# - Repository access: this repo
# - Repository permissions: Actions (read and write), Metadata (read)
#
# NOTE: No GitHub "Secrets" read/write permission is required for these helpers.
#
# Self-hosted runner notes (macOS + Docker Desktop):
# - By default the runner is started in DinD mode (`INSTAFY_RUNNER_DOCKER_MODE=dind`) so CI steps
#   that use bind-mounts from the workspace (docker compose, etc) work reliably.
# - You can force host-socket mode with `INSTAFY_RUNNER_DOCKER_MODE=socket`, but on macOS it will
#   usually fail with "mounts denied" for paths under `/actions-runner/_work/...`.
#
# Tip: to keep CI isolated from your local dev stack (so you can run `pnpm stack:up` while CI runs),
# leave `INSTAFY_RUNNER_NETWORK` unset so the runner container uses the default bridge network.
#
# Default: run a single runner (recommended).
INSTAFY_RUNNER_COUNT=1
#
# To run more than one CI job at a time, start multiple runners (each runner handles 1 job):
# INSTAFY_RUNNER_COUNT=2
#
# (Advanced) Base volume name for DinD cache. Runner #2, #3, ... will suffix the index automatically:
# INSTAFY_RUNNER_DIND_VOLUME=instafy-gh-runner-dind
#
# (Recommended) Persistent pnpm store cache (dramatically speeds up `pnpm install` on self-hosted):
# INSTAFY_RUNNER_PNPM_STORE_VOLUME=instafy-gh-runner-pnpm-store
# INSTAFY_RUNNER_PNPM_STORE_DIR=/pnpm-store
GH_TOKEN=
